&lt;h2 id="configuring-gpio-inputs">Configuring GPIO Inputs&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>The YardForce NX types use GPIO-based sensors for wheel lift detection, stop buttons, and collision detection.
These must be configured before the robot is operational.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>There is currently no dedicated hardware-specific &lt;code>inputs.yaml&lt;/code> for NX types yet.
As a starting point, use the &lt;a href="https://github.com/ClemensElflein/open_mower_ros/blob/main/src/open_mower/params/hardware_specific/YardForceSA_OEM/inputs.yaml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SA/SC types definition&lt;/a>
as a template and adjust it to your wiring.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Refer to &lt;a href="https://openmower.de/archive/v1.3.0/archive/v1.3.0/docs/knowledge-base/configuration/configure-gpio-inputs/">Configuring GPIO Inputs&lt;/a>
for detailed instructions
– including the Hall-MUX selection required for Carrierboard ≥ 1.2.0.&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>